PUBLIC SERVICES COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Public Services Committee was held on Tuesday, December 17, 2024, in
Committee Room 104 and via electronic meeting, staring at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were
as folLows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Scott Roybal, Chairman: Pete Layboum; Dr. Mark Rinne; and Tom
Segrave.
AGENDA ITEMS
ANNOUNCEMENT:
For calendar year 2025, starting Monday, January 6, 2025, the Public
Services Committee will meet on Monday’s at 12:00 p.m. (noon) and the Finance Committee will
meet on Tuesday’s at 12:00 p.m. (noon) in Room 104 of the Municipal Building at 2101 O’Neil
Avenue. (On the Pt and 3 Monday and Tuesday of each month.)
18.
ORDINANCE 3rtj READING
— Amending subsections 6.6.3.b.3, 6.7.5.c, and 6.9.4.e of
the Unified Development Code (UDC), changing building façade design requirements for
multifamily residential development.
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 3’ and final reading, seconded by Mr. Laybourn. Motion died
with Mr. Laybourn and Mr. Segrave voting “NO” and Dr. Rinne voting “YES.”
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and noted no changes
since approval on 2nd reading. Committee member Segrave commended on the item and provided
information related to various siding building materials.
20.
ORDINANCE —3 READING
Amending Chapter 8.68, Camping on Public Property, of
the Municipal Code of the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, expanding the gcneral prohibition
on camping to all public property of the City, creating a permitting process, making
conforming amendments and repealing obsolete provisions.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on 3fh and final reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried
by unanimous voice vote.
Richard Johnson, Ward III Councilman and sponsor of the item, advised there have been no
changes since approval on 2d reading and committee member Layboum commented on the item.
21.
ORDINANCE _2od READING
— Annexing to the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, land
located north of Cheyenne Street and west of and adjacent to Ridge Road. (SPONSOR
—
MR. ROYBAL)
Mr. Segrave moved to approve on
2T1L1 reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
