23.
ORDINANCE 2nd READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne establishing the zoning classification of AG Agricultural for land being annexed
to the City at Lot I, Block 1, North Range Substation, Laramie County, Wyoming (located
south of Happy Jack Road, west of Bruns Way). (SPONSOR
— MR. ROYBAL)
Mr. Laybourn moved to approve on 2”d reading, seconded by Dr. Rinne. Motion carried by
unanimous voice vote.
Seth Lloyd, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report.
24.
ORDINANCE
READING
— Amending the Official Zoning Map of the City of
Cheyenne establishing the zoning classification of AG Agricultural for land located
northeast of the intersection of West Allison Road and Walterscheid Boulevard.
(SPONSOR - MR. ROYBAL)
Dr. Rinne moved to approve on 2nd reading, seconded by Mr. Segrave. Motion died with Mr.
Laybourn and Mr. Segrave voting “NO” and Dr. Rinne voting “YES.”
Connor White, Planning & Development Department, provided a staff report and noted the
proposed ordinance is to assign a City zone to previously (in 1980) annexed land. Charles Bloom,
Planning & Development Department Director, and Stefanie Boster, City Attorney, provided
additional information. John Sayers, developer’s representative, provided information related to
the proposed zoning. Committee members Laybourn, Rinne, and Segrave commented on the item.
Ward Ill Councilwoman, Dr. Aldrich, also commented on the item. Public comments were made
by Nancy Evagelatos, Lee Filer, and Ashley Singleton.
25.
